Task: Your task is to complete a set of classes for musical instruments. You need to properly implement inheritance and then demonstrate polymorphism by overriding the `makeSound()` method in the `Guitar` and `Piano` subclasses to produce instrument-specific sounds.

Submitted code:
```
class MusicalInstrument {
  constructor(brand) {
    this.brand = brand;
  }

  makeSound() {
    // This method should ideally be overridden by subclasses.
    return `${this.brand} makes a generic instrument sound.`;
  }
}

class Guitar extends MusicalInstrument {
  constructor(brand) {
    // TODO: Call the parent class constructor using 'super()'
    // TODO: Make sure 'brand' is passed correctly
    super();
    this.brand = brand;
  }

  makeSound() {
    // TODO: Override this method to return a specific guitar sound
    // It should include the brand, e.g., "Fender Guitar plays a strumming sound."
    return this.brand + " Guitar plays a strumming sound.";
  }
}

class Piano extends MusicalInstrument {
  constructor(brand) {
    // TODO: Call the parent class constructor using 'super()'
    // TODO: Make sure 'brand' is passed correctly
    super();
    this.brand = brand;
  }

  makeSound() {
    // TODO: Override this method to return a specific piano sound
    // It should include the brand, e.g., "Steinway Piano plays a melodic tune."
    return this.brand " Piano plays a tune.";
  }
}

// Test cases (already present, player doesn't modify)
const genericInstrument = new MusicalInstrument("GenericBrand");
console.log(genericInstrument.makeSound());

const electricGuitar = new Guitar("Fender");
console.log(electricGuitar.makeSound());

const grandPiano = new Piano("Steinway");
console.log(grandPiano.makeSound());

```

